// 46_rop_loop.cwiz - a ROP program that keeps running.
//
// What it does:
//   Loops forever: clears the screen, draws a diagonal line, prints a label
//   and renders the buffer.  It never returns, so the screen keeps being
//   refreshed.
//
// How to run it:
//   1. Build this file in the Wiz tab of CasioEmuMsvc (the "#rop" directive
//      selects the gadget-chain backend).
//   2. Inject the payload at E9E0 ("#org E9E0" below).
//   3. In the calculator's program mode press LEFT, then EXE.
//   4. The loop runs until the program is aborted with AC.
//
// Every ROP program starts with setlr() and setsfr(); this example calls
// screen_del() inside the loop so that every frame starts from a clean
// screen.  render() is mandatory after drawing.
//
// About the key check:
//   The ROP gadget database does contain key-reading gadgets (getkey at
//   0x2F5EA, getscancode at 0x1F24E and check_any_key_pressed__ at 0x0E826),
//   but they are not part of the documented high-level API: getkey needs the
//   address of a 2-byte keycode slot and the keycode has to be matched
//   against a table (cmp_ea), and neither of those is exposed here.  This
//   example therefore sticks to the documented API (print / line / render /
//   screen_del) and simply keeps looping.
//
//   To make the loop terminate on a key press, the program needs a global
//   counter in the backup area plus the "[er8]+=er2" gadget (0x09CA0) and
//   the +4784 backup offset - see section 4.2 of
//   docs/rop-notes/rop-580-guide.txt.
#rop
#for 580
#org E9E0
#launcher common

int main() {
    setlr();
    setsfr();

    while (1) {
        screen_del();

        line(0, 0, 191, 62);
        print(0x30, 0x01, "ROP LOOP");

        render();
    }
}
